{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0429","billNumberShort":"H.B. 429","billNumberLong":"HB0429S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0613","shortTitle":"Special Districts Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"PIERUC","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Pierucci, Candice B.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MCCAYD","floorSponsorName":"Sen. McCay, Daniel","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses withdrawal of a county or a municipality from a special district under certain circumstances.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms and modifies definitions;<hr><ltbullet>provides a process for a county of the first class to initiate withdrawal from a first responder district;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the process to conduct a feasibility study on withdrawal from a first responder district;<hr><ltbullet>creates a process for a county of the first class or a municipality located in a county of the first class to initiate withdrawal from a garbage disposal district;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits a garbage disposal district from incurring debt, issuing bonds, or otherwise incurring a financial obligation for a period of time after the county or municipality initiates the process to withdraw from the garbage disposal district;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes a county or municipality and a garbage disposal district to enter into an agreement to withdraw;<hr><ltbullet>describes the requirements for a county or municipality to complete withdrawal from a garbage disposal district absent an agreement, including:<hr><ltbullet1>conducting a feasibility study;<hr><ltbullet1>conducting a public hearing on the proposed withdrawal;<hr><ltbullet1>providing notice of a public hearing on the proposed withdrawal; and<hr><ltbullet1>adopting a resolution to withdraw;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the process to file with the lieutenant governor certain documents;<hr><ltbullet>describes the process to determine the effective date of a withdrawal; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"RuthAnne Oakey-Frost","fiscalAnalyst":"Timothy Kevin Bereece","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/23/2026","trackingID":"GTRSHPVGND","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 08:38:58.637","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 08:38:58.637","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for HB0429","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2026-01-30 08:39:00.693","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill sent to agencies for fiscal input for HB0429","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Agency","actionDate":"2026-01-30 08:39:00.693","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA2","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"House/ received bill from Legislative Research","owner":"Clerk of the House","actionDate":"2026-01-30 09:53:30.000","actionClass":"H","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"HRECLRGC","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"House/ 1st reading (Introduced)","owner":"House Rules Committee","actionDate":"2026-01-30 11:52:09.000","actionClass":"H","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"HREAD1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note sent to sponsor for HB0429","owner":"Version Sponsor","actionDate"